{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--ro-marks-hortative-mood","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--cohortative"],"statement":{"en":"The sentence-final particle ro expresses hortative/cohortative meaning ('let's...').","ja":"終助詞 ro は勧誘（「〜しよう」）を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ro"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0050-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0051-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--shizunai-hortative-marked-by-na","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In the Shizunai dialect, the hortative mood is expressed by adding the sentence-final particle na to the predicate, indicating a mutual invitation or light inclusive command.","ja":"静内方言において、勧誘法は述語に終助詞 na を付加することで表され、話者を含めた相互の勧誘または穏やかな命令を示す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["na"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0199-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--saru-uses-ro-for-hortative","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Shizunai uses na whereas Saru uses ro for hortative expressions."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--saru-uses-ro-for-hortative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--particles"],"statement":{"en":"In the Saru dialect, the particle ro is used to express the hortative function.","ja":"沙流方言では勧誘機能を表すために ro が用いられる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ro"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-03","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0199-03","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--ro-marks-hortative-mood","differs_in":"scope","note":"Refsing reports the hortative use of ro specifically for the Saru dialect."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--the-hortative-sentence-final-na-is-probably-identical","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--boundaries"],"statement":{"en":"The hortative sentence-final na is probably identical with the sentence-final na derived from the conjunctionalizer na implying an unstated order or admonition.","ja":"勧誘の文末詞 na は、言外の命令や訓戒を暗示する接続詞化接辞 na に由来する文末詞 na とおそらく同一である。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["na"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0199-04","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--the-particle-ro-is-an-imperative-particle-directed","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--cohortative"],"statement":{"en":"The particle ro is an imperative particle directed to the first-person plural ('let us...').","ja":"ro は第一人称複数に対する命令（let us...）である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ro"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0165-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--the-particle-ro-is-most-frequently-placed-after","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--cohortative"],"statement":{"en":"The particle ro is most frequently placed after fourth-person plural verbs to invite someone ('let's...'), but Tamura (1988a) notes it can be used with other persons, showing examples with first-person singular and third person.","ja":"助詞 ro は多くの場合4人称複数形の動詞の後に置かれて「〜しましょう」と誘う意味を表すが、田村 (1988a) では他の人称でも用いられるとして1人称単数形や3人称とともに使われた例が示されている。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ro"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0331-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--the-phrase-itak-an-ro-expresses-let-s","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--cohortative"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase itak-an ro expresses 'let's talk'.","ja":"itak-an ro という表現は「話そう」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["itak-an ro"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:ono2022@handbook-epub/l0078-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--the-modern-expression-iku-an-ro-is-used","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--cohortative"],"statement":{"en":"The modern expression Iku-an ro! is used to mean 'Let's drink together' as a toast.","ja":"現代の表現 Iku-an ro! は乾杯の際に「一緒に飲もう」という意味で用いられている。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["modern usage"]},"forms":["iku-an ro"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:ono2022@handbook-epub/l0080-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--the-particle-ta-functions-to-mark-optative-wishing","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The particle ta functions to mark optative/wishing sentences, and clauses with this ta can also end with okai.","ja":"助詞 ta は願望の係りとして機能し、okai をもって結ぶこともある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ta","okai"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0151-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--the-sentence-final-okai-expresses-strong-desire","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The sentence-final okai expresses strong desire.","ja":"文末の okai は強い願望を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["okai"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0168-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--the-particle-oka-correlates-with-the-emphatic-adverbial","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The particle oka correlates with the emphatic adverbial particle ta in a kakari-musubi-like manner to express an optative wish ('if only...', 'I wish I could...').","ja":"助詞 oka は強調の副助詞 ta と係り結びのように呼応して、「〜すればいいのに」「〜したいものだ」という願望を表わす。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["oka","ta"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0333-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--in-sentence-final-position-na-may-also-have","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In sentence-final position, na may also have a hortative function.","ja":"文末位置において、naは勧誘的機能を持つこともある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":["in sentence-final position"]},"forms":["na"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0246-12","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--in-chitose-ainu-ro-can-also-be-used","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--particles"],"statement":{"en":"In Chitose Ainu, ro can also be used in clauses with a first-person singular subject and a second-person singular object.","ja":"千歳方言でも、ro が1人称単数主格-2人称単数目的格で用いられた例がある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ro"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0331-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:tam/hortative-and-optative--to-express-the-cohortative-meaning-let-s-do","revision":1,"topic":"topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topics":["topic:tam/hortative-and-optative","topic:tam/hortative-and-optative--particles"],"statement":{"en":"To express the cohortative meaning 'let's do (something)', the final particle ro is used in Saru, Chitose, Horobetsu, Yakumo, Asahikawa, Nayoro, and Sōya; rok is used in Asahikawa, Nayoro, and Obihiro; and no is used in Urakawa and Samani.","ja":"勧誘（「〜しよう」）の意味を表す終助詞として、沙流・千歳・幌別・八雲・旭川・名寄・宗谷では ro、旭川・名寄・帯広では rok、浦河・様似では no が用いられる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ro","rok","no"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0051-22","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
